# Step 28, its third pull request's first part: custom commands, the
# review's fix M1. Headless mode takes a command from the words after `-p`
# alone, never from standard input, and never one whose name holds a `/`;
# with standard input it sends the command and that text together, and the
# core puts the text after the command's expanded text, as one prompt, and
# refuses anything but text beside a command. Broken one at a time, with
# the tests that must fail. `a-command-takes-an-image-beside-it` takes the
# place of `a-command-comes-with-a-prompt` in `step-28-commands.breaks`,
# whose rule (nothing beside a command) this fix changed.

[break] headless-reads-a-command-from-standard-input
rule: Headless mode takes a command from the words after `-p` alone: what standard input gives, a log or an issue's body, is text for the model, whatever its first line is.
file: crates/cineris-cli/src/headless.rs
in: Prompt::command
find: let named = self.words.strip_prefix('/')?;
replace: let named = self.piped.strip_prefix('/').or_else(|| self.words.strip_prefix('/'))?;
caught-by:
    cineris-cli::bin/cineris headless::tests::a_piped_prompts_first_line_is_never_a_command

[break] headless-takes-a-path-for-a-commands-name
rule: A name that holds a `/` is never a command, as the interface reads it: `/usr/bin/ld: cannot find -lfoo` given after `-p` is a linker's line, for the model.
file: crates/cineris-cli/src/headless.rs
in: Prompt::command
find: !name.contains('/')
replace: true
caught-by:
    cineris-cli::bin/cineris headless::tests::the_linkers_line_is_never_a_command

[break] headless-drops-standard-input-beside-a-command
rule: With a command and standard input, headless mode sends both in `turn/start`: the command, and what standard input gave in `input`, for the core to put after the command's text.
file: crates/cineris-cli/src/headless.rs
in: Prompt::start
find: vec![Part::text(self.piped.clone())]
replace: Vec::new()
caught-by:
    cineris-cli::bin/cineris headless::tests::a_command_with_piped_input_sends_both

[break] a-commands-text-drops-what-came-with-it
rule: The text sent with a command in `turn/start` follows the command's expanded text, after a blank line, in the one prompt that is recorded and that `prompt.submit` sees.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/core.rs
in: Core::handle_op
find: let input = if after.trim().is_empty() {
replace: let input = if true || after.trim().is_empty() {
caught-by:
    cineris-core::it commands::file_commands_are_listed_expanded_and_refused_with_reasons

[break] a-command-takes-an-image-beside-it
rule: A command in `turn/start` takes text beside it and nothing else: an image is refused `invalid_prompt`, and no turn starts.
file: crates/cineris-core/src/core.rs
in: Core::handle_op
find: .any(|part| !matches!(part, cineris_protocol::Part::Text(_)))
replace: .any(|part| matches!(part, cineris_protocol::Part::Text(_)) && false)
caught-by:
    cineris-core::it commands::file_commands_are_listed_expanded_and_refused_with_reasons
